{"name":"Historic Shade","hex":"#ada791","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"historic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Very important; noteworthy: having importance or significance in history.","Old-fashioned, untouched by modernity."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A history, a non-fiction account of the past.","A historian."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/historic"},{"term":"shade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Darkness where light, particularly sunlight, is blocked.","Something that blocks light, particularly in a window."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To shield (someone or something) from light.","To shield oneself from light."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shade"}],"entries":[{"title":"History","blocks":[{"text":"History is the systematic study of the past, focusing primarily on the human past. As an academic discipline, it analyses and interprets evidence to construct narratives about what happened and explain why it happened. Some theorists categorize history as a social science, while others see it as part of the humanities or consider it a hybrid discipline. Similar debates surround the purpose of history—for example, whether its main aim is theoretical, to uncover the truth, or practical, to learn lessons from the past. In a more general sense, the term history refers not to an academic field but to the past itself, times in the past, or to individual texts about the past."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Carstian_Luyckx_-_Still_life_with_a_globe%2C_books%2C_shells_and_corals_resting_on_a_stone_ledge.jpg/330px-Carstian_Luyckx_-_Still_life_with_a_globe%2C_books%2C_shells_and_corals_resting_on_a_stone_ledge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History"},{"title":"Tint, shade and tone","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, a tint is a mixture of a color with white, which increases lightness, while a shade is a mixture with black, which increases darkness. A tone is produced either by mixing a color with gray, or by both tinting and shading. Mixing a color with any neutral color reduces the chroma, or colorfulness, while the perceived hue can be affected slightly."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Tint-tone-shade.svg/330px-Tint-tone-shade.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tint%2C_shade_and_tone"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/POxy_v0017_n2099_a_01_hires_-_cropped.jpg/500px-POxy_v0017_n2099_a_01_hires_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/POxy_v0017_n2099_a_01_hires_-_cropped.jpg/500px-POxy_v0017_n2099_a_01_hires_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fragment of the Histories by Herodotus, an Ancient Greek historical text[24]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APOxy_v0017_n2099_a_01_hires_-_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Collections_Archive%2C_St._Petersburg_Museum_of_History%2C_St._Petersburg%2C_FL.jpg/500px-Collections_Archive%2C_St._Petersburg_Museum_of_History%2C_St._Petersburg%2C_FL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Collections_Archive%2C_St._Petersburg_Museum_of_History%2C_St._Petersburg%2C_FL.jpg/1280px-Collections_Archive%2C_St._Petersburg_Museum_of_History%2C_St._Petersburg%2C_FL.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Collections_Archive%2C_St._Petersburg_Museum_of_History%2C_St._Petersburg%2C_FL.jpg/500px-Collections_Archive